{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A tool for creating games that can handle large numbers of on-screen units. Games can run on PC, mobile, and the web.  </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Scene Editor</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Supports various tile sizes (16\u2013256px). Add actors, regions, lights, animations, particles, parallax images, and tile maps. Includes a built-in 2D lighting system. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >UI Editor</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Design UI layouts and interactions visually. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Animation Editor</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Create frame-by-frame and particle animations. Supports paper doll and multi-directional animations (1, 2, 4, 8 directions).  </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Particle Editor</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple and easy to use; create particle effects for weather, skills, and more.<br>  </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Custom Attributes</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Add custom attributes to actors, skills, states, equipment, and items. Implement functionality via events or scripts.  </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >High-performance; supports low-code development and TypeScript for game scripting</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Open-source on GitHub</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Games\u00a0Released on Steam</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Border Pioneer -\u00a02346410</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Journey to the West Survivor -\u00a02450100</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What a Shitty Job -\u00a03278480</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Moka Future -\u00a01779760</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Other</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The author is currently developing a Unity game and rarely updates this editor.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/1964480?t=1763646129","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_as